1: # Keyboard
2: Simple library to listen for keystrokes from the keyboard
3: 
4: The code is inspired by [termbox-go](https://github.com/nsf/termbox-go) library.
5: 
6: ### Installation
7: Install and update this go package with `go get -u github.com/eiannone/keyboard`
8: 
9: ### Usage
10: Example of getting a single keystroke:
11: 
12: ```go
13: char, _, err := keyboard.GetSingleKey()
14: if (err != nil) {
15:     panic(err)
16: }
17: fmt.Printf("You pressed: %q\r\n", char)
18: ```
19: 
20: Example of getting a series of keystrokes with a blocking `GetKey()` function:
21: ```go
22: package main
23: 
24: import (
25: 	"fmt"
26: 	"github.com/eiannone/keyboard"
27: )
28: 
29: func main() {		
30: 	if err := keyboard.Open(); err != nil {
31: 		panic(err)
32: 	}
33: 	defer func() {
34: 		_ = keyboard.Close()
35: 	}()
36: 
37: 	fmt.Println("Press ESC to quit")
38: 	for {
39: 		char, key, err := keyboard.GetKey()
40: 		if err != nil {
41: 			panic(err)
42: 		}
43: 		fmt.Printf("You pressed: rune %q, key %X\r\n", char, key)
44:         if key == keyboard.KeyEsc {
45: 			break
46: 		}
47: 	}	
48: }
49: ```
50: 
51: Example of getting a series of keystrokes using a channel:
52: ```go
53: package main
54: 
55: import (
56: 	"fmt"
57: 	"github.com/eiannone/keyboard"
58: )
59: 
60: func main() {
61: 	keysEvents, err := keyboard.GetKeys(10)
62: 	if err != nil {
63: 		panic(err)
64: 	}
